# LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# server.mjs starts with a shebang and npm's launcher execs it directly on
# Linux and macOS. If Git hands out CRLF line endings, that first line becomes
# "#!/usr/bin/env node\r" and the kernel looks for an interpreter literally
# named "node\r": the failure reads "bad interpreter: no such file or
# directory", which names neither Git nor the line ending.
#
# Windows checkouts get LF too. Every editor that matters handles it, and it
# keeps what is committed identical to what is published.
* text=auto eol=lf
